{"archetypes":[{"name":"oos-flow","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff rewires accepted OOS artifacts across tally, emit, review-and-fix, and gate paths.","prompt_body":"Trace the accepted out-of-scope artifact lifecycle across tally-code-votes.sh, emit-tally.sh, review-and-fix.sh, accumulated-oos.md, and oos-accepted-review.md. Check that every producer writes canonical OOS headers, that emit preservation cannot drop or rebuild accepted scope-drift blocks, and that parent/tmpdir mirrors remain consistent across standalone and implement modes. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"shell-parsers","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The change depends on bash and awk block parsing, header rewriting, and sequence counting.","prompt_body":"Inspect the bash and awk parsing logic for block boundaries, header normalization, result filtering, and monotonic OOS sequence counts. Pay special attention to multiline blocks, body text that looks like headings, missing files, stdin versus file input, and Bash 3.2 or BSD portability assumptions. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"parity","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The awk and Python OOS counters must remain semantically aligned for disposition gates.","prompt_body":"Compare the legacy-header and security-exclusion semantics in python/oos.py with skills/implement/scripts/oos-non-security-block-count.awk and their tests. Look for regex mismatches, tag requirements, security field handling differences, and cases where one implementation would count a block that the other ignores. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"security-routing","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff expands security tag detection and must not leak security OOS items into public sinks.","prompt_body":"Review the changed security-routing detectors in lib-vote-tally.sh and oos-serialize.sh and how their results control accepted OOS sinks. Check for false negatives that could publish security-tagged findings and false positives that could suppress ordinary public OOS cleanup. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"harness-contracts","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"New helpers and altered contracts require Makefile, docs, and regression harnesses to exercise the production path.","prompt_body":"Examine whether the new normalize helper contract, Makefile target placement, and updated harnesses cover the production tally-to-emit overwrite chain and coder-skipped append path. Check that documented behavior matches script behavior and that tests assert the critical sink preservation, canonical headers, dual-sink aliasing, and fallback serialization cases. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
